  "steps": [
    {"title": "A command arrives", "say": "`redis-cli` sends **RESP**: an array of three bulk strings. The server's main thread sits in its **event loop**, waiting for any socket to wake it.", "show": ["send"], "flow": ["send"], "notes": [{"on": "send", "text": "*3 $3 SET $8 greeting $5 hello", "side": "top"}]},
    {"title": "The socket wakes the loop", "say": "The socket turns readable, so the loop runs the handler set at connect time, `readQueryFromClient`. It appends the bytes to the client's **query buffer**.", "show": ["readable"], "flow": ["readable"], "focus": ["reader"], "notes": [{"on": "loop", "kind": "tag", "text": "io-threads 1 by default", "tone": "info"}]},
    {"title": "Bytes become arguments", "say": "`processInputBuffer` sees the leading `*`, and `processMultibulkBuffer` cuts it into three string objects. A half-arrived command just waits for the next read.", "show": ["parse"], "flow": ["parse"], "focus": ["parser"], "notes": [{"on": "parser", "text": "argv = SET, greeting, hello", "side": "top"}]},
    {"title": "A name becomes a function", "say": "Still during parsing, `preprocessCommand` looks `SET` up in the `server.commands` dict and checks its arity, so a bad command is flagged before anything runs.", "show": ["lookup"], "flow": ["lookup", {"edge": "lookup", "reverse": true, "packet": "setCommand"}], "focus": ["table"], "notes": [{"on": "table", "text": "set → setCommand, arity -3", "side": "bottom"}]},
    {"title": "The gatekeeper", "say": "`processCommand` checks auth, ACL permissions and, if set, `maxmemory` (SET is DENYOOM). Only then does `call()` jump into `setCommand`.", "show": ["run", "exec"], "flow": ["run", "exec"], "focus": ["gate"], "notes": [{"on": "gate", "kind": "tag", "text": "-NOPERM · -OOM", "tone": "warn"}]},
    {"title": "The key is written", "say": "`setGenericCommand` stores `greeting` in the keyspace. Its `server.dirty++` is how `call()` knows to propagate the SET to the AOF and replicas.", "show": ["write"], "flow": ["write"], "focus": ["keys"], "notes": [{"on": "keys", "text": "new key → dbAddByLink", "side": "bottom"}]},
    {"title": "Reply now, send later", "say": "`addReply` only copies `+OK` into the client's buffer and queues the client. Just before the loop sleeps, `beforeSleep` writes it straight to the socket.", "show": ["reply", "flush"], "flow": ["reply", "flush"], "focus": ["outq"], "notes": [{"on": "outq", "text": "write handler only if it won't fit", "side": "left"}]},
    {"title": "SET, end to end", "say": "Read, parse, look up, check, run, store, reply. Commands execute one at a time on the main thread, so no two writes ever interleave.", "recap": true, "flow": ["send", "readable", "parse", "lookup", "run", "exec", "write", "reply", "flush"]}
  ],
  "spacing": 1.15
}
